{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And with Aharon HaShem was very wrathful to destroy him.</b> Known is what the Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted of this verse: this destruction was the obliteration of sons, as it says (Amos 2:9) ״ואשמיד פריו ממעל ושרשיו מתחת״ — and I destroyed his fruit from above and his roots from beneath; and since Moshe prayed, he made his prayer half. And in any case this verse, written in the Torah as a sign and a wonder, is that Aharon sinned in the calf a great sin, until he was punished for it with the obliteration of sons; and surely one must wonder, for Aharon intended it for the sake of Heaven, and his thought was pure in the service of the Blessed Name; and behold, the verse says (Exodus 32:21) ״אשר עשה אהרן״ — 'that Aharon did' — it holds him to account only for the deed alone, not for the thought; if so, why was HaShem wrathful with him? And the answer to this is that the Holy One, blessed be He, is exacting with the righteous even to a hair's breadth, as the Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted from what is written (Psalms 50:3) ״וסביביו נשערה מאד״ — 'and around Him it is very stormy' (read: He is exacting to a hair's breadth); and even though his intention was for the sake of Heaven, in any case the deed of Aharon with the hands was a profanation of the Name, and even though he himself did not sin in it, behold, he caused Israel to sin unintentionally, for through him they went astray after it and many of Israel fell; and so Moshe reminded him (Exodus 32) ״כי הבאת עליו חטאה גדולה״ — 'for you have brought upon him a great sin.' And a great proof that he did not sin in it at all is from what Moshe mentioned in his reproofs and said (Deuteronomy 33:8) ״תריבהו על מי מריבה״ — 'You will contend with him at the waters of Merivah'; and he called him חסיד (Psalms 50) — pious — for no other sin was found in him; and there I shall write, with the help of the Name."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:47:10.065243795Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}